5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I think we should focus on the actual problems we face daily, not just the flashy ideas.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,"Agreed, Daisuke. Flashy ideas often ignore the humans doing the work. Let’s keep it grounded and practical.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Grounded is fine, but I’m tired of promises based on assumptions. We need to verify the actual constraints before committing to anything.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,Shunichi is right. We must verify constraints. I worry about where the money actually comes from before we commit to anything flashy.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I agree with Shunichi. We need to check the records of past rollouts to see what actually worked before we spend more money.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m worried we’re missing the small, daily losses. Can we look at the time lost to copying records?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, exactly. That copying waste is a symptom of ignoring real staffing limits. I’ll dig into the coordination group’s staffing too.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, staffing is internal. I care about external dependencies. Who’s checking network coverage at customer plants?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, external coverage matters, but I need to know the capital budget and software allowance first. That determines what is actually affordable for us.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, budget is vital, but I’m worried about repeating past mistakes. I’ll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts to see what actually survived.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I’ll look into the time lost to copying records and the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,I’ll check the coordination group’s staffing and in-house developer availability. We can’t just assume people are free to absorb extra work.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,I’ll examine network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability. We can’t promise dates if the infrastructure or people aren’t actually ready.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I will examine the capital budget and software allowance, plus vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work. I need to know the true cost before we commit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I’ll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. I need to see if we’re just repeating the same mistakes.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m a bit nervous, but I hope the incident logs show the real daily pain. Let’s see what we find.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,I’m curious to see if the staffing data proves my hunch. Let’s hope the numbers back up my gut feeling.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let’s hope the data confirms my suspicion that we’re building castles on sand. I’ll see you all in the next round.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will wait for the data. Knowing the true cost is essential before we proceed.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m really hoping the files show a clear pattern. If we keep ignoring history, we’re just wasting everyone’s time and energy.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
