35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The logs show eleven misrouted deliveries, all from duplicate addresses. Plus, we lose an hour daily copying records. This is real, daily pain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that daily hour is brutal. But my findings are worse: two people are doing everyone’s coordination work by hand, and our devs are locked away until Q3.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, that confirms my worst fear. Half the customer sites lose signal for afternoons, and our devs are buried until Q3. We are completely unprepared.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital line is frozen, but software allowance remains. Vendor licences climb per head, while fixed-fee rates held steady. We must avoid per-head traps.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that budget news is tough. But my files show a pattern: broad tools get abandoned, while narrow, single-trade tools survive. We must avoid the ""everyone"" trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that pattern explains the misroutes. If we stop copying and fix the address mismatch, we save that daily hour.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, fixing addresses is a band-aid. My data shows the coordination group is drowning. We need to stop assuming those two people have infinite time.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, drowning is a symptom. The real killer is that half our sites are offline afternoons. We can’t build on a foundation that literally disappears.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, offline sites are critical, but my data shows per-head licences are a trap. Fixed-fee work is stable. We must avoid recurring costs that escalate with headcount.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, offline sites are a hard stop. But my data shows narrow tools survive. We need a small, specific fix, not a massive platform that everyone ignores.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I hear you. But if we fix the address mismatch, the copying stops. That’s the immediate relief for the floor.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, relief is nice, but it ignores the human cost. We can’t keep burning out those two coordinators. We need a solution that respects actual capacity.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, capacity is a constraint, not a solution. We can’t hire our way out of dead zones. The infrastructure gap is the hard blocker.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, infrastructure is vital, but I worry about the renewal bill. If we ignore the frozen capital line, next year’s costs will crush us.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I agree. But my data proves narrow tools survive. We need a small, specific fix, not a massive platform that everyone ignores.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m quiet, but I worry. If we ignore the daily copying, the floor keeps bleeding time. Please, let’s not forget the small, real losses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, infrastructure is vital, but people are the bottleneck. We can’t fix dead zones if our coordinators are already drowning. Let’s respect their limits.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, people are the symptom, not the cause. If the signal dies, no amount of staffing saves the delivery. We must fix the infrastructure first.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I stand by the budget reality. We cannot afford escalating per-head costs. We must choose a fixed-fee solution that respects the frozen capital line.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m worried we’re repeating history. My data shows broad tools fail, but narrow ones survive. Let’s pick a small, specific fix that actually sticks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
